    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1140">

                <pb facs="0942" n="826" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg826"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/4692</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-08-22T13:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 22, 1912—1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In the States of Morelos, Mexico, Puebla, Oaxaca, Michoacán and Guerrero
                    conditions are as bad as at any time during the two revolutions, if not worse;
                    disorders becoming more general; violence of the most barbarous character daily
                    occurring. The Government, apparently incompetent to meet the situation, is
                    losing what little prestige it gained from victories in the north. I urge the
                    most rigid precautions relative to the State of Sonora where the Chihuahua
                    barbarities will doubtless be repeated in worse forms and on a larger scale.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
